---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Why your business email should end in your own name | JayTech9"
  description="A Gmail address is free, but an email on your own domain costs very little and makes customers trust you more. Here's what it takes in Ghana."
  ogType="article"
>
  <article>
    <header class="page-head">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="crumb">
          <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>
        </p>
        <h1>Why your business email should end in your own name</h1>
        <p class="meta">
          <time datetime="2026-10-25T00:00:00.000Z">25 October 2026</time>
          <span>Business</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="wrap section post-body">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Most small businesses in Ghana start with an address like <code>mybusiness2024@gmail.com</code>. It
          works, it’s free, and nobody stops you. But when a customer is choosing between you and a
          competitor, <code>info@mybusiness.com</code> quietly tells them you’re established and here to stay.
        </p>
        <h2 id="what-it-costs">What it costs</h2>
        <p>You need two things: a domain name and somewhere for the email to live.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>A .com domain</strong> costs roughly $10–11 a year at registrars that don’t add a markup,
            which is about GH₵ 115–130 depending on the exchange rate. Watch out for registrars that charge a
            few cedis for the first year and then three or four times more to renew.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Email forwarding</strong> can be free. Services like Cloudflare Email Routing send
            everything addressed to <code>info@yourbusiness.com</code> straight to the Gmail you already use.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A full inbox</strong> that can also send from the new address is free on some plans for
            small teams, or about $1 per person per month on paid plans.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>So for around GH₵ 120 a year, you can look like a company rather than a side project.</p>
        <h2 id="three-mistakes-to-avoid">Three mistakes to avoid</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Signing up with the new address.</strong> Log in to your domain account with an email you
          already control, such as your personal Gmail. If the domain ever lapses, you don’t want the password
          reset to go to an inbox that no longer works.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Letting it expire.</strong> Turn on auto-renew and keep the card on file valid. When a
          domain lapses, someone else can buy it, along with every customer who still emails you there.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Registering it in someone else’s name.</strong> If a web designer buys your domain for you,
          make sure it’s registered to you or your business. You should be able to log in and see it yourself.
        </p>
        <h2 id="where-to-start">Where to start</h2>
        <p>
          Pick a short name that matches your business, check it’s available, and buy it in your own name.
          Then point your email at it before you print it on anything. If you’d like help setting it up,{' '}
          <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a> and we’ll walk you through it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  <section class="contact-band" aria-labelledby="contact-band-heading">
    <div class="wrap contact-band__inner">
      <div class="contact-band__text">
        <h2 id="contact-band-heading">Want help setting this up?</h2>
        <p>
          Start with a free 30-minute call. We’ll listen, suggest what would help, and send a written quote
          with a clear timeline.
        </p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button contact-band__primary" href="/contact/">
            Book a free call
          </a>
          <a class="button button--quiet contact-band__quiet" href="https://wa.me/233203651974">
            Chat on WhatsApp
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <svg class="contours contact-band__art" viewBox="0 0 600 600" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <circle cx="40" cy="560" r="18" class="contours__dot"></circle>
        <path
          d="M 110 560 A 70 70 0 0 0 40 490"
          pathLength="1"
          class="contours__arc contours__arc--green"
          style="--delay:0ms"
        ></path>
        <path
          d="M 158 560 A 118 118 0 0 0 40 442"
          pathLength="1"
          class="contours__arc contours__arc--blue"
          style="--delay:70ms"
        ></path>
        <path
          d="M 206 560 A 166 166 0 0 0 40 394"
          pathLength="1"
          class="contours__arc contours__arc--blue"
          style="--delay:140ms"
        ></path>
        <path
          d="M 254 560 A 214 214 0 0 0 40 346"
          pathLength="1"
          class="contours__arc contours__arc--green"
          style="--delay:210ms"
        ></path>
        <path
          d="M 302 560 A 262 262 0 0 0 40 298"
          pathLength="1"
          class="contours__arc contours__arc--blue"
          style="--delay:280ms"
        ></path>
        <path
          d="M 350 560 A 310 310 0 0 0 40 250"
          pathLength="1"
          class="contours__arc contours__arc--blue"
          style="--delay:350ms"
        ></path>
        <path
          d="M 398 560 A 358 358 0 0 0 40 202"
          pathLength="1"
          class="contours__arc contours__arc--green"
          style="--delay:420ms"
        ></path>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head h1 {
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .crumb {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .meta {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
  }
  .post-body {
    padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
  }
  .contours {
    width: 100%;
    overflow: visible;
  }
  .contours__arc {
    fill: none;
    stroke-width: 2.5px;
    stroke-linecap: round;
  }
  .contours__arc--blue {
    stroke: var(--blue);
  }
  .contours__arc--green {
    stroke: var(--green);
    stroke-width: 4px;
  }
  .contours__dot {
    fill: var(--green);
  }
  .contours--animate .contours__arc {
    stroke-dasharray: 1;
    stroke-dashoffset: 1px;
    animation: 0.9s cubic-bezier(0.3, 0.6, 0.2, 1) forwards draw;
    animation-delay: var(--delay);
  }
  @keyframes draw {
    to {
      stroke-dashoffset: 0;
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .contours--animate .contours__arc {
      stroke-dashoffset: 0;
      animation: none;
    }
  }
  .contact-band {
    background: var(--blue);
    color: var(--white);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .contact-band__inner {
    align-items: end;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem);
    display: grid;
  }
  .contact-band__text {
    max-width: 34rem;
  }
  .contact-band h2 {
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
  .contact-band p {
    color: #dcecf5;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-block: 1.25rem 2rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .contact-band__primary {
    background: var(--white);
    border-color: var(--white);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .contact-band__primary:hover {
    background: var(--paper);
    border-color: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .contact-band__quiet {
    color: var(--white);
    border-color: var(--white);
  }
  .contact-band__quiet:hover {
    background: var(--white);
    border-color: var(--white);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .contact-band .contact-band__art {
    display: none;
  }
  .contact-band .contact-band__art .contours__arc--blue {
    stroke: #4d9cc8;
  }
  @media (width>=52rem) {
    .contact-band__inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 1fr;
    }
    .contact-band .contact-band__art {
      justify-self: end;
      max-width: 22rem;
      margin-bottom: -6rem;
      display: block;
    }
  }
</style>
